-29828" :question/problem "Find the antiderivative of $\\sqrt{x^{5}} + \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{x^{5}}}$."}] :knowledge-point/title "Computing an Integral Using the Sum Rule"} {:knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186184002 :question/id #uuid "ea7dadee-2b44-5e62-bef4-26fb0cb185ea" :question/is-example true :question/math-academy-id "e-372" :question/problem "Calculate $\\displaystyle \\int 2 x^3 - x \\,\\textrm d x$." :question/worked-solution "Using the sum and constant factor rules, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\int2x^{3} - xdx &= 2\\intx^{3}dx - \\intxdx \\\\\n&= 2(\\frac{x^{3 + 1}}{3 + 1}) - (\\frac{x^{1 + 1}}{1 + 1}) + C \\\\\n&= 2(\\frac{x^{4}}{4}) - (\\frac{x^{2}}{2}) + C \\\\\n&= \\frac{x^{4}}{2} - \\frac{x^{2}}{2} + C\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a58c0a18-4221-50f1-b31c-ae58d099d79d" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048426}] :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186184489 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8121efaa-aeec-5e91-a61d-727d740bc028" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6x^{4} + \\frac{5x^{4}}{2} + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186181375} {:answer/id #uuid "92aab1b4-6f6e-5fab-a6a9-b59142f9faf4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3x^{4} + \\frac{5x^{3}}{2} + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186181376} {:answer/id #uuid "f24f92fe-e32b-5c6c-8d02-97902921dc09" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12x^{2} + \\frac{5x^{2}}{2} + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186181377} {:answer/id #uuid "44324091-9605-52af-a6eb-fd647cfc8423" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3x^{4} + \\frac{5x^{2}}{2} + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186181378} {:answer/id #uuid "6e593588-5dad-5897-b45b-4a265b859e18" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3x^{2} + \\frac{5x^{2}}{2} + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186181379}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "44324091-9605-52af-a6eb-fd647cfc8423" :answ